+# Main repository rule port — 2026-10-19
+
+The isolated lane `lane/dk-rules-main-sync` starts at `8ba4981`. It ports the
+reviewed rule repair from `lane/dk-rules-portable` (`c7367f0`), with its final
+container-mount clarification. Canonical rules will live at `x0x37/docs` after
+this lane fast-forwards `smk37`. The firmware integration task keeps its separate
+source and running validation.
+
+The main repository lacked most current enforcement tools. The port adds the
+reviewed tools and their existing support scripts and fixtures. It also brings
+the guarded installer from the existing firmware lineage, unchanged, so current
+rules do not point to an installer without gate, foreground, lock, and head
+checks. No firmware, Bluetooth source, asset, host source, or build script changes.
+The older main test runner and product docs remain; the runner adds six standalone
+rule checks, and BUILDING adds only the reviewed validation section and notice.
+
+Checks on the port:
+
+- Native Mac current preference lint: 4/4. Rule rollout scratch test: PASS.
+- Native Mac docs folder quickcheck with an unwritable shared cache path: PASS.
+- Linux `x0x37-validation:local`, network disabled: portable checks 5/5;
+  rule quickcheck 10/10; device regression evidence 9/9; exact install evidence
+  guard 21/21; foreground and hardware lock guards 11/11.
+- Independent port review: compared 113 rule, tool, test, and fixture files with
+  the reviewed lane; no source mismatch. Current links resolve. No firmware diff.
+- First `/workspace` mount failed before tests because linked worktree metadata
+  retained host paths. The successful run mounted the workspace at the same
+  absolute path. BUILDING now documents this or an independent container clone.
+
+These are development checks and mocked guard checks. No device was opened.
+No full firmware gate, install, or device PASS is claimed. Exact asd-ste and
+caveman originals remain unavailable as recorded in SKILLS.md.
