+# Applied rule rollout — 2026-10-19
+
+The main repository `smk37` fast-forwarded to `2815062` through the isolated
+`lane/dk-rules-main-sync` lane. It now holds the maintained rules and their
+validation support. No firmware source, Bluetooth source, asset, host source,
+library, or build script object changed from `8ba4981`.
+
+Applied rollout: 70 workspace files and two live temporary-worktree entry points.
+All 36 first-party checkout entries inside the workspace resolve. The two live
+temporary checkouts, `/private/tmp/b1wt` and
+`/private/tmp/x0x37-dk-batch11-status`, now point to the same current workspace
+entry. Prunable old worktrees and `refs-oscuro` were left alone. No finished task
+was restarted for rollout.
+
+All 72 written files match their recorded hashes. Every replaced file has its
+exact prior bytes in the backup. The [machine-readable record](rollout-2026-10-19.json)
+names the backup folder and changes. A repeated dry run reports zero changes.
+All 14 archived rule records still match the original inventory hashes.
+
+Only recognized repair wording changed in the three installed Mac hooks. Their
+clone/history and proprietary-reference guard behavior remains intact. Push
+destinations remain disabled or approved local paths. The portable full runner
+is available in maintained source; no Linux build runner was imposed on Mac
+pushes. Firmware source and the ongoing frozen validation run were untouched.
+
+After the main commit, native docs quickcheck passed, as did current preference
+lint and the rollout regression. The independent main-port review and Linux
+rule/install checks passed before integration. These are development checks,
+not firmware release or keyboard evidence.
+
+The firmware integration task retains branch order and its frozen source. Its
+repair lane is `lane/dk-rules-portable`: commits `c7367f0` and `9995a71`. It can
+take those rule and enforcement changes with its next integration step. A
+generated workspace `AGENTS.md` may be locally modified in older checkouts; its
+prior version and generated hash are in the rollout manifest. Preserve unrelated
+changes when replacing that generated entry with the canonical committed entry.
+
+The first coordination notice reached the firmware chat. Automatic approval
+review blocked a second notice because messaging requires approval and the
+tool's approval policy is `never`. It was not retried. This record is the
+concrete handoff; no unconfirmed message is claimed as sent.
+
+Exact `asd-ste` and `caveman` originals remain unavailable. Their authenticated
+source files or box export are the remaining skill dependency. All entry points
+state that limit and require plain, correct, brief English in all project output.
+
+A fresh read-only subagent followed the actual `ux_combined_review` and temporary
+`b1wt` entry links after rollout. It found the current authority and skill status,
+resolved all followed links, and described a complete Mac docs task without a
+box, keyboard, or retired-role loop. It made no edits or validation claims.
-- 
